WEBVTT

welcome-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
Hello Margaret.

welcome-2
00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:06.154
This video helps you get ready for your cataract surgery (right eye) at Brackenridge.

welcome-3
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:08.077
It takes about two minutes.

welcome-4
00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:13.462
You can pause it, turn on captions, or ask a question at any time.

what-happens-1
00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:19.615
The cloudy lens in your right eye is removed and replaced with a clear artificial lens.

what-happens-2
00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:20.769
You'll be awake.

what-happens-3
00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:24.615
The area will be numbed, so you shouldn't feel pain.

what-happens-4
00:00:24.615 --> 00:00:29.231
It's a day case, so you should go home the same day.

when-where-1
00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:31.923
Your appointment is on Thursday 12 November.

when-where-2
00:00:31.923 --> 00:00:33.462
Please arrive at 8:30am.

when-where-3
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:37.692
Go to the Eye Day Unit, Level 1, Brackenridge Community Hospital.

when-where-4
00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:41.154
Expect to be with us for about 3 hours.

eating-normally-1
00:00:41.154 --> 00:00:41.923
Good news.

eating-normally-2
00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:45.000
You don't need to stop eating or drinking.

eating-normally-3
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.231
You can have your meals as normal before you come in.

medicines-1
00:00:49.231 --> 00:00:50.385
Now, your medicines.

medicines-2
00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:54.615
Keep taking your usual medicines, including eye drops, unless told otherwise.

medicines-3
00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:58.077
If you take blood-thinning medicines, call the pre-assessment team.

medicines-4
00:00:58.077 --> 00:01:00.385
Do not stop them without advice.

what-to-bring-1
00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:05.385
Please bring a list of your medicines, your glasses and something to read.

what-to-bring-2
00:01:05.385 --> 00:01:07.692
Leave jewellery and valuables at home.

going-home-1
00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:10.385
You'll need someone to take you home.

going-home-2
00:01:10.385 --> 00:01:15.769
Do not drive until your eye doctor says your sight meets the legal standard.

going-home-3
00:01:15.769 --> 00:01:19.231
Most people notice clearer sight within a few days.

going-home-4
00:01:19.231 --> 00:01:22.692
Use your eye drops as shown for 4 weeks.

warning-signs-1
00:01:22.692 --> 00:01:33.462
After you get home, call us straight away if you have any of these: increasing pain in the eye; your sight gets worse; increasing redness or sticky discharge.

contact-1
00:01:33.462 --> 00:01:41.154
If you have a question, type it in the box next to this video, or call us on 01632 960215.

contact-2
00:01:41.154 --> 00:01:43.462
Outside office hours, call 01632 960999.

contact-3
00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:46.154
We look forward to seeing you, Margaret.
